<title>UK: Saudi tells OPEC supply at quota in Jan - OPECNA.</title>
<headline>Saudi tells OPEC supply at quota in Jan - OPECNA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia told OPEC it produced 8.005 million barrels per day (bpd) in January, in line with its eight million bpd quota, the OPEC News Agency said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The kingdom, OPEC and the world's largest oil producer, said supply to the market was slightly higher at 8.006 million bpd.</p>
<p>Supply, as defined by OPEC, is calculated as domestic consumption, plus net export sales of crude and products, plus withdrawals of stocks held outside national boundaries.</p>
<p>Production and supply data for the month of January received so far by the OPEC Secretariat from member countries is as follows (in thousand bpd):  </p>
<p>COUNTRY	  PRODUCTION	SUPPLY     QUOTA</p>
<p>-------	  ----------	------     -----</p>
<p>INDONESIA     1,328.2		--	1,330.0</p>
<p>KUWAIT	  2,005.7		--	2,000.0</p>
<p>LIBYA	   1,393.0		--	1,390.0</p>
<p>QATAR	     399.1		--	  378.0</p>
<p>SAUDI ARABIA  8,005.1	   8,006.1    8,000.0</p>
<p>VENEZUELA     2,405.0		--	2,359.0</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7630</p>
</text>
